A tank is filling at a constant rate. Find the filling rate in L/min. If this rate continues, how much water will the tank contain at 12 minutes?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.65cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (8,6);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(8.5,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,6.5);
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \p/\v in {1/10,2/20,3/30,4/40,5/50,6/60} {\draw[black] (0,\p)--(-0.1,\p);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\p) {$\v$};}
\draw[graphBlue,thick] (0,2)--(8,6);
\fill[graphBlue] (0,2) circle (2pt);
\fill[graphBlue] (8,6) circle (2pt);
\node at (4,-0.85) {Time (minutes)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.8,3) {Volume (L)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph shows a tank draining at a constant rate. Find its signed gradient and its rate of decrease in volume. How many minutes after $t=0$ will it be empty if this rate continues?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=0.8cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (6,6);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.5,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,6.5);
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \p/\v in {1/20,2/40,3/60,4/80,5/100,6/120} {\draw[black] (0,\p)--(-0.1,\p);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\p) {$\v$};}
\draw[graphBlue,thick] (0,6)--(6,3);
\fill[graphBlue] (0,6) circle (2pt);
\fill[graphBlue] (6,3) circle (2pt);
\node at (3,-0.85) {Time (minutes)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.15,3) {Volume (L)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A container fills, pauses, then fills again. Find the filling rate during each of the three stages.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.45cm,y=0.75cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridGrey,very thin,xstep=2,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (12,6);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(12.7,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,6.5);
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10,12} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \p/\v in {1/10,2/20,3/30,4/40,5/50,6/60} {\draw[black] (0,\p)--(-0.15,\p);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.15,\p) {$\v$};}
\draw[graphBlue,thick] (0,0)--(4,4)--(6,4)--(12,6);
\foreach \pt in {(0,0),(4,4),(6,4),(12,6)} {\fill[graphBlue] \pt circle (2pt);}
\node at (6,-0.9) {Time (seconds)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-2.6,3) {Volume (L)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A tank drains at two different constant rates. Find the rate of decrease during the second stage, from $4$ to $10$ minutes.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.55cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridGrey,very thin,xstep=2,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (10,9);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(10.7,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,9.5);
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \p/\v in {2/20,4/40,6/60,8/80,9/90} {\draw[black] (0,\p)--(-0.15,\p);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.15,\p) {$\v$};}
\draw[graphBlue,thick] (0,9)--(4,6)--(10,3);
\foreach \pt in {(0,9),(4,6),(10,3)} {\fill[graphBlue] \pt circle (2pt);}
\node at (5,-0.9) {Time (minutes)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.5,4) {Volume (L)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two hoses fill identical empty buckets. The lines share the same axes. Find each filling rate and state which hose fills faster.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.85cm,y=0.85cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{graphRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (6,5);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.5,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,5.5);
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \p/\v in {1/3,2/6,3/9,4/12,5/15} {\draw[black] (0,\p)--(-0.1,\p);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\p) {$\v$};}
\draw[graphBlue,thick] (0,0)--(6,5);
\draw[graphRed,thick,dashed] (0,0)--(6,3);
\fill[graphBlue] (6,5) circle (2pt);
\fill[graphRed] (6,3) circle (2pt);
\node[text=graphBlue,above left] at (5,4.17) {Hose A};
\node[text=graphRed,below right] at (4,2) {Hose B};
\node at (3,-0.85) {Time (minutes)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.1,2.5) {Volume (L)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A tank starts with some water and fills at the constant rate shown. Its capacity is $180$ L. How many minutes after $t=0$ will it reach capacity? Assume the rate continues until it is full.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.85cm,y=0.85cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (6,6);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.5,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,6.5);
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.1);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \p/\v in {1/20,2/40,3/60,4/80,5/100,6/120} {\draw[black] (0,\p)--(-0.1,\p);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\p) {$\v$};}
\draw[graphBlue,thick] (0,1.5)--(6,6);
\fill[graphBlue] (0,1.5) circle (2pt);
\fill[graphBlue] (6,6) circle (2pt);
\node[right] at (0.15,1.5) {$30\text{ L}$};
\node at (3,-0.85) {Time (minutes)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.1,3) {Volume (L)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
